From: Realme X2 Pro Linux port
Subject: [PATCH] gst: allow the CPU camera launcher to request owned frame copies

The display consumer can retain shared buffers across multiple camera frames.
Keep the upstream default unless this process explicitly opts into CPU copies.
This requires the upstream deferred-recycle lock-order fix in 0001.

--- a/src/gst/gstpipewiredeviceprovider.c
+++ b/src/gst/gstpipewiredeviceprovider.c
@@ -41,6 +41,14 @@ gst_pipewire_device_create_element (GstDevice * device, const gchar * name)
                 "fd", pipewire_dev->fd, NULL);
   g_free (serial_str);
 
+  /* A per-process CPU camera profile; other clients retain upstream defaults.
+   * Reconfigure only changes the target of this same source element, so this
+   * property remains in effect when the application switches cameras. */
+  if (GST_IS_PIPEWIRE_SRC (elem) &&
+      gst_device_has_classes (device, "Video/Source") &&
+      g_strcmp0 (g_getenv ("SAMURAI_CAMERA_COPY"), "1") == 0)
+    g_object_set (elem, "use-bufferpool", FALSE, NULL);
+
   return elem;
 }
 
